dosbox-x Borland-Clipper-Microsoft
==================================


USEFUL LINKS
------------

* https://winworldpc.com/
* https://archive.org


INSTALLATION
------------

You can install dosbox-x by means of

    sudo apt install dosbox-x

The `RetroProgramming` repository can be installed in your home directory (`~`) in either of the following ways.

* Option 1: Clone the repository with Git

    cd ~
    git clone https://github.com/Pynckels/RetroProgramming.git
    chmod +x ~/RetroProgramming/dosbox-x.sh

* Option 2: Download and extract the repository as a ZIP file

    unzip RetroProgramming-main.zip
    mv RetroProgramming-main RetroProgramming
    chmod +x ~/RetroProgramming/dosbox-x.sh

CONFIGURATION
-------------

To configure the dosbox-x, you can edit the file

    ~/RetroProgramming/dosbox-x.conf


STARTUP
-------

To start this retro programming dosbox: execute (run) the file

    ~/RetroProgramming/dosbox-x.sh

This can be done from the command line interface (terminal) or from the file manager in the graphical user interface.
